---
title: Color generator
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Turns text into hex colors, three characters to each color, or reads a message back out of a palette.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>The colors are shown both as a list of hex colors and as blocks of color. Each color holds three characters of the text as three bytes of hex (red, green and blue), shown under it. Padding adds extra characters when the hex can't make up all 6 characters of the last color, and padded colors are marked with *.</p>
    <p>"Colors to text" goes the other way: paste hex colors, with or without #, to get the text back. Padding at the end is dropped. "Save as image" downloads the colors as a picture, one block each.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Colors", placeholder = "Example: Hello → #48656C #6C6FFF", layout = "analysis") %}
<div class="btn-group" role="group" aria-label="Convert">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Encode" aria-pressed="true">Text to colors</button>
    <button class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Decode" aria-pressed="false">Colors to text</button>
</div>
<div class="input-group w-auto" data-colors-padding>
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Padding">Padding</label>
    <select class="form-select" id="{{ filename }}Padding" autocomplete="off">
        <option value="F" selected>F padding</option>
        <option value="0">0 padding</option>
    </select>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
